#* {{quote-book|en|year=1930|author=William Faulkner|title=As I Lay Dying|publisher=Library of America|year_published=1985|page=67|passage="He would have '''rid''' that horse, too," pa says, "if I hadn't a stopped him. A durn spotted critter wilder than a catty-mount. A deliberate flouting of her and me."}}

